      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! Timbre is determined by the unique combination of overtones in addition to the fundamental frequency produced by an instrument. When you hear a flute playing, it's not just the fundamental pitch that resonates, but also a series of overtones generated by the harmonics of the vibrating air column within. These overtones contribute to the flute’s distinctive sound quality and add richness and character. Different materials and shapes of the instrument will produce varying overtones, thus giving each flute its unique timbre.",
